1
00:00:00,640 --> 00:00:02,520
(Sheldon(Knock, knock, knock):)This is for you.

2
00:00:03,143 --> 00:00:04,523
(Penny:)Hello, Sheldon.

3
00:00:05,061 --> 00:00:06,641
(Howard:)Hi.

4
00:00:09,232 --> 00:00:11,732
- What is this?
- It's a questionnaire I devised.

5
00:00:11,901 --> 00:00:14,781
(Sheldon:)I'm having some difficulty bonding
with a colleague at work...

6
00:00:14,946 --> 00:00:19,366
(Sheldon:)...so I'm doing a little research to better
understand why my current friends like me.

7
00:00:20,452 --> 00:00:23,452
(Penny:)Yes, well, that is a good question.

8
00:00:23,621 --> 00:00:26,161
(Penny:)But is this really the best way
to figure it out?

9
00:00:26,333 --> 00:00:27,543
(Sheldon:)I agree.

10
00:00:27,709 --> 00:00:29,499
(Sheldon:)The social sciences are largely hokum.

11
00:00:29,669 --> 00:00:33,339
(Sheldon:)But short of putting electrodes in your brain
and monitoring your response...

12
00:00:33,506 --> 00:00:36,596
(Sheldon:)...to my companionship,
this is the best I can do.

13
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:38,430
Okay, question one:

14
00:00:38,595 --> 00:00:42,345
"Rank the following aspects
of Sheldon Cooper in order of appeal:

15
00:00:42,515 --> 00:00:45,265
(Penny:)Intelligence,
ruthless attention to hygiene...

16
00:00:45,435 --> 00:00:48,935
...playfulness, Java-applet writing"?

17
00:00:50,523 --> 00:00:53,233
(Sheldon:)I know. I may have started off
with a fairly obvious one.

18
00:00:53,401 --> 00:00:55,651
(Sheldon:)An aspect
of my most appealing trait:

19
00:00:55,820 --> 00:00:57,820
(Penny:)playfulness.

20
00:00:57,989 --> 00:01:01,279
Why don't you rank that number one?
You're on your own for the rest.

